import{_ as t,o as i,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 261 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Qualification as Enlightened Predator: Good Will Does Not Change the Predatory Structure","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 261 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Qualification as Enlightened Predator: Good Will Does Not Change the Predatory Structure","no":261,"module":2,"tags":["Tang-Luo","Enlightened Predator","Predatory Structure","Good Will","Myriad-Realms Benchmark"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise","19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries","01-Anchor Symbiotic Civilization Manifesto"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0261_模块2-唐罗-开明掠夺者定性.md","filePath":"en/0261_模块2-唐罗-开明掠夺者定性.md"}'),a={name:"en/0261_模块2-唐罗-开明掠夺者定性.md"};function s(r,e,l,d,u,g){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-261-tang-luo-decomposition-qualification-as-enlightened-predator-good-will-does-not-change-the-predatory-structure" tabindex="-1">Entry 261 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Qualification as Enlightened Predator: Good Will Does Not Change the Predatory Structure <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-261-tang-luo-decomposition-qualification-as-enlightened-predator-good-will-does-not-change-the-predatory-structure" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 261 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Qualification as Enlightened Predator: Good Will Does Not Change the Predatory Structure&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Tang-Luo System (Entry 11)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-why-good-people-are-also-classified-as-predators" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Why good people are also classified as predators <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-why-good-people-are-also-classified-as-predators" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Why good people are also classified as predators&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the anti-predation axiom defines predation not by moral motive, but by structure: &quot;developing increments, not consuming stocks; Great Dao public at all tiers, no private hoarding, no monopoly.&quot; Tang Luo&#39;s personal conduct is nearly perfect, but the structure he established still falls within the predation genealogy. This entry takes the law-first axiom as core, formally completing Tang Luo&#39;s qualification as &quot;enlightened predator.&quot; Protagonist uniqueness dependency judgment: <strong>Tang Luo = high dependency / bestowal-style civilization</strong>. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The enlightened predator&#39;s energy-level waste is a kind of &quot;moral premium&quot; waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Goodwill premium</strong>: because Tang Luo is a good person, all beings tend to overestimate the system he established, ignoring its structural defects. This cognitive bias of &quot;because he is good so the system is good&quot; lets civilization miss the institutional reform window</li><li><strong>Reform misread</strong>: every good-will adjustment Tang Luo makes is cheered as &quot;the sage lord is merciful,&quot; not &quot;institutions finally progressed.&quot; The causal chain of reform is stealthily swapped from &quot;institutions need it&quot; to &quot;the benefactor bestows it&quot; — next reform must wait for the benefactor&#39;s mood again</li><li><strong>Morality substituting analysis</strong>: because Tang Luo&#39;s morality is impeccable, no one dares make &quot;structural critique&quot; of his system. Criticizing a good person is politically incorrect. So structural problems are covered by moral praise</li></ul><p>Energy-level waste: <strong>a good person&#39;s goodness became the best decoration for the system&#39;s wall.</strong> This is the most hidden waste — the wall is warm, so no one wants to tear it down.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Critical aphasia</strong>: because Tang Luo is too good, any criticism of his system seems &quot;ungrateful.&quot; Civilization loses its self-critical ability; structural problems ferment in silence</li><li><strong>Expectation misalignment</strong>: all beings expect &quot;the next good policy,&quot; not &quot;a set of institutions that automatically produce good policies.&quot; Expecting the wrong object, the reform direction is forever wrong</li><li><strong>Moral hostage</strong>: if later generations want to rewrite Tang Luo&#39;s bestowals into institutions, they will be accused of &quot;distrusting the sage lord&quot; and &quot;wanting to take the sage lord&#39;s credit.&quot; The road of institutional reform is sealed off by Tang Luo&#39;s own moral aura</li></ol><p>Regression form: under the sage lord&#39;s moral light, civilization even loses the language system of &quot;getting better.&quot;</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>&quot;Enlightened predator&quot; complete definition:</p><ul><li><strong>Predation form</strong>: knowledge monopoly, racial exclusion, bestowal attachment, single-point decision-making</li><li><strong>Enlightened manifestation</strong>: truly well-intentioned, profit-sharing with all beings, not bloodthirsty, not luxurious, caring for people&#39;s livelihood</li><li><strong>Key judgment</strong>: whether enlightened or not does not change predation&#39;s structure; it only changes predation&#39;s temperature. An ice wall is a wall, a warm wall is also a wall</li></ul><p>Three layers of Tang Luo&#39;s predatory thinking:</p><ol><li><strong>He himself may not realize it</strong>: he thinks he is &quot;liberating all beings,&quot; actually &quot;organizing all beings to attach&quot;</li><li><strong>His good will is real</strong>: not a disguise, not hypocrisy</li><li><strong>But structure&#39;s power exceeds personal good will</strong>: as long as he stands on the predatory system&#39;s ceiling, all his good deeds are just repainting the predatory system</li></ol><p>By the Gu Chensha / Tang Luo judgment table standard: Tang Luo = <strong>enlightened predator</strong>, alongside &quot;predators&quot; (e.g., bloodthirsty-type protagonists) and &quot;oligarchic predators&quot; (e.g., patriciate-type protagonists), but with the lowest predation temperature and mildest toward all beings. Qualifying him as predator is not cursing him, but saying — his goodness has not yet penetrated his position.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Enlightened Predation</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Goodwill profit-sharing</td><td>Institutional rights confirmation, profit-sharing need not rely on good will</td></tr><tr><td>Warm wall</td><td>Tear down the wall</td></tr><tr><td>Critical aphasia</td><td>Anchor Supervision Committee institutionalizes criticism, not depending on personal courage</td></tr><tr><td>Morality substituting analysis</td><td>Law-first: ask structure first, then motive</td></tr><tr><td>Bestowal-style reform</td><td>Legislation-style reform, every progress written into statutes</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Alternative&#39;s crux: Heng Yuan Zhou does not deny Tang Luo&#39;s good, but requires his good to &quot;upgrade&quot; — from personal virtue to civilizational law.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate Tang-Luo system, marking &quot;goodwill premium&quot; variables</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: Group A maintains enlightened predation; Group B writes all Tang Luo&#39;s good deeds into the constitution</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: civilization self-critical ability, institutional reform frequency, long-term prosperity index</li><li><strong>Review expectation</strong>: Group B self-critical index significantly higher than Group A, long-term prosperity curve flatter and longer</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium-high</strong>. &quot;Good-person protagonist&quot; is self-consistent within its world-view</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: medium</strong>. Long-form writing&#39;s greatest challenge to a &quot;perfect good-person protagonist&quot; is: late must create enemies for him, create setbacks, create moral dilemmas. Each creation requires breaking early &quot;he never makes mistakes&quot; settings — retcon</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: high. This entry is the formal proclamation of this qualification</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: goodwill premium covers structural defects, wasting the reform window</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: being enlightened does not change predation structure, a warm wall is still a wall</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo is &quot;the kindest predator,&quot; but kindness does not change position</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: good will covers those seen, institutions cover 99%</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: cross-plane governance cannot rely on good will, must rely on laws</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Tang Luo is not a bad person — on this point Heng Yuan Zhou is more certain than anyone. But precisely because he is a good person, his system is deceptive — a warm wall is more dangerous than an ice wall, because no one wants to tear it down. The enlightened predator&#39;s final way out is not becoming kinder, but stepping down from the predator&#39;s position and dismantling the position itself.</p><p>In the final analysis, Tang-Luo · qualification as enlightened predator described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise</a> · <a href="./19-修炼伦理与边界.html">19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries</a> · <a href="./01-锚点共生文明宣言.html">01-Anchor Symbiotic Civilization Manifesto</a></li></ul>',32)])])}const m=t(a,[["render",s]]);export{c as __pageData,m as default};
